            <ArticleTitle>Enormous right coronary arterial aneurysm in a patient with type IV Ehlers-Danlos syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>259-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient with a giant aneurysm in the right coronary artery combined with dilated and tortuous left descending and circumflex arteries is described. The clinical features and implications are discussed.</AbstractText>
